Dear friends,

Frank and I intend to start a discussion group about the concepts
of the future LaTeX.  This group should consist of a small number
of people that have some experience in document design or TeX/LaTeX
programming (or even better, in both of these subjects).  The
discussions are to be held mainly by means of electronic mail, with
casual meetings when the need arises.

The main topics in the near future should be the goals for version
2.10, namely the design of a new style file interface, discussions
about the properties of meta document styles (like proccedings), etc.

We are asking you whether you are interested in joining us.

If you are interested, we have two further questions:
1) Are you able to set up a mail redistribution service on your
   machine?
2) Do you have sufficient disk space to archive the messages of
   the discussion group?

At the moment I don't see how this could be done on Frank's or my
host.

   Awaiting your answers,
      Rainer & Frank



